{"id":"a17eb400-a1ef-42a3-8e4a-60a24fdd0499","object":"chat.completion","created":1784884791,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if 'tokens' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing required fields: tokens and calls')\\n    tokens = case['tokens']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(tokens, list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in tokens):\\n        raise ValueError('tokens must be a list of strings')\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError('calls must be a list')\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not all(k in call for k in ('call_id','start','end','score','replacement_tokens')):\\n            raise ValueError('Each call must have call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens')\\n        if not isinstance(call['call_id'], str) or not isinstance(call['start'], int) or not isinstance(call['end'], int):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid call fields')\\n        if not isinstance(call['replacement_tokens'], list):\\n            raise ValueError('replacement_tokens must be a list')\\n\\n    # Rank calls: descending score, then ascending start, then ascending call_id\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda c: (-c['score'], c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n\\n    selected = []\\n    # intervals as (start, end)\\n    selected_intervals = []\\n    for call in sorted_calls:\\n        s, e = call['start'], call['end']\\n        # Check overlap with any selected interval\\n        overlap = False\\n        for sel_s, sel_e in selected_intervals:\\n            if max(s, sel_s) < min(e, sel_e):\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append(call)\\n            selected_intervals.append((s, e))\\n\\n    # Order selected calls by start ascending for reporting\\n    selected.sort(key=lambda c: (c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected]\\n\\n    # Apply replacements from right to left (descending start)\\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)\\n    for call in sorted(selected, key=lambda c: -c['start']):\\n        s, e = call['start'], call['end']\\n        replacement = call['replacement_tokens']\\n        result_tokens[s:e] = replacement\\n\\n    return {'selected_call_ids': selected_call_ids, 'tokens': result_tokens}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that takes a payload with tokens and calls, applies the logic: rank calls by descending score, then start, then call_id. Greedily pick non-overlapping calls based on start/end intervals (assuming inclusive start, exclusive end? The example: call a start=1 end=3, b start=2 end=5. They overlap. The algorithm should reject overlaps. Replacement tokens are inserted at the start position, replacing the span from start to end-1? The tokens array has indices 0..9. The calls specify replacement_tokens. We need to produce interleaved token stream: token sequence with replaced spans replaced by their replacement_tokens. Apply replacements from right to left so earlier offsets don't shift. That means process calls in descending order of start? Actually \"right to left\" means process from highest start to lowest, because when you replace a later span, earlier indices are unaffected. But we also have the order of accepted calls: we need to output selected_call_ids (the IDs of accepted calls) and tokens (the final interleaved token sequence). The procedure:\n\n1. Validate: case has tokens (list of strings), calls (list of dicts with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). All required. If missing, raise ValueError.\n\n2. Rank calls by (score descending, start ascending, call_id ascending? The spec: \"Rank candidates by descending score, start position, then call ID.\" So sort key = (-score, start, call_id). But note: start position is used as tiebreaker for ranking. But greedy selection uses the sorted order. For overlap detection, intervals: start inclusive, end exclusive? The examples: call a start=1 end=3 covers indices 1,2 (tokens at positions 1 and 2). call b start=2 end=5 covers indices 2,3,4. They overlap at index 2. So they overlap if max(start1,start2) < min(end1,end2). We'll assume half-open [start,end). So if two calls have start and end the same? Not present.\n\n3. Greedy: iterate sorted calls, if current call's interval does not overlap with any previously selected call, select it.\n\n4. After selecting calls, sort them by start position ascending to apply replacements from right to left? Wait: \"Order accepted calls by source start for reporting.\" That's for reporting selected_call_ids? Or for applying replacements? The spec says: \"Apply replacements from right to left so earlier offsets do not shift.\" So we need to apply replacements in descending order of start position. But for reporting selected_call_ids, we should order them by source start (ascending). So output selected_call_ids sorted by start ascending (and if tie, maybe call_id? The spec says \"by source start for reporting\", so start ascending. If multiple calls have same start? Probably not, but we can break ties by call_id.\n\n5. Build resulting tokens: start with the original tokens list. For each selected call in descending order of start: replace the sublist tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens. That's a slice. Then after all replacements, we get the final tokens list.\n\n6. Return {\"selected_call_ids\": list of call_ids in ascending start order, \"tokens\": final list of strings}.\n\nEdge cases: Calls with replacement_tokens empty? Possibly but we assume they exist. If no calls selected, selected_call_ids empty, tokens original.\n\nWe must not mutate input case.\n\nImplementation in Python, using standard library.\n\nWrite solve(case) as described.\n\nNow produce JSON output: {\"implementation\": \"Python source code as string\"}.\n\nWe need to escape the source for JSON: newlines as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, quotes as \\\".\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1654,"completion_tokens":1385,"total_tokens":3039,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":795},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":118},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}